$date
  WaveCrux annotation demo fixture
$end
$version
  hand-authored for the waveform annotations example
$end
$comment
  A deliberately tiny handshake trace for exercising waveform annotations.

  Identifier codes are assigned in ascending ASCII order matching declaration
  order (! " # $ %), because the backend numbers signalRefs by identifier-code
  order rather than declaration order — the committed session's refs only line
  up with the names if those two orders agree.

  `bus` holds 8'ha3 across tick 500, which is the value the demo session's
  annotations were witnessed against. Change that value (edit the `b10100011 $`
  line at #400 to any other pattern) and reopen the session: the annotation
  anchored to `top.bus` will render DRIFTED, which is the whole point of the
  witness mechanism.

  `spare` is deliberately NOT in the demo session's displayed signal list, so
  the annotation anchored to it exercises the orphan path.
$end
$timescale 1 ns $end
$scope module top $end
$var wire 1 ! clk $end
$var wire 1 " req $end
$var wire 1 # ack $end
$var wire 8 $ bus $end
$var wire 1 % spare $end
$upscope $end
$enddefinitions $end

#0
0!
0"
0#
b0 $
0%
#100
1!
#200
0!
1"
#300
1!
#400
0!
b10100011 $
#500
1!
1#
#600
0!
#700
1!
0"
0#
#800
0!
1%
#900
1!
#1000
0!
